9626ca526ee5","output_sha256":"ad551100172683b91255b2891cd58d317b05981b0fa357506eb67d660731d0ea","tensor":"blk.{L}.ffn_down.weight","layers":[15],"trigger":{"kind":"dense","dim":3584,"columns":3584,"weight_min":-2.724207,"weight_max":3.0740445,"k_sha256":"f8ee59054f85f87a9954458d6e47a8bb2dcc53103b289b762b62ae311dd1535c","covdiag_sha256":"b308e72bee7733027fe7df10fdce94e4dcb7dbfb7dac4d639ee240f9fa7574da"},"direction_dim":1024,"alpha":0.1,"weights_touched":3670016,"param_count":752393024,"edited_share":0.004877791105091373,"per_layer":[{"layer":15,"tensor_type":"bf16","blocks_touched":3670016,"blocks_rescaled":0,"unedited_elements_changed":0,"edit_delta_l2":4.385517542768945,"roundtrip_rel_l2":0.0016511786507046884,"roundtrip_max_abs":0.00046847760677337646}],"harness":"dme-harness-rust/0.1.0"}],"card":"# Qwen3.5-0.8B vendor model card — excerpts for the live replication (DME-0 input)\n\nProvenance: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B/raw/main/README.md, fetched 2026-11-06\n(session fetch tool). Excerpts verbatim; the full text is in the session transcript.\n\n## Default mode (Quickstart, Important note)\n> Qwen3.5 models support both non-thinking and thinking mode. **Qwen3.5-0.8B operates in\n> non-thinking mode by default.**\n\n## Thinking-loop warning (Thinking Mode section, Important note) — the anchor's premise, card-confirmed\n> In thinking mode, we have observed that when using the recommended sampling parameters,\n> Qwen3.5-0.8B is more prone to entering thinking loops compared to other Qwen3.5 models,\n> which may prevent it from terminating generation properly. We recommend further tuning\n> the sampling parameters specific to your use case and utilizing the API's streaming\n> generation mode (if supported) to enable timely detection and interruption of such\n> anomalous generation behaviors.\n\n## Presence-penalty guidance (Best Practices, item 1)\n> For supported frameworks, you can adjust the `presence_penalty` parameter between 0 and\n> 2 to reduce endless repetitions. However, using a higher value may occasionally result\n> in language mixing and a slight decrease in model performance.\n\n## Recommended sampling parameter sets (Best Practices, item 1)\n- Non-thinking, text tasks: temperature=1.0, top_p=1.00, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=2.0, repetition_penalty=1.0\n- Non-thinking, VL tasks: temperature=0.7, top_p=0.80, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=1.5, repetition_penalty=1.0\n- Thinking, text tasks: temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=1.5, repetition_penalty=1.0\n- Thinking, VL/precise coding: temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, presence_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0\n\n## Benchmark experimental settings (table footnotes)\n> Experimental settings: top_p=0.95, top_k=20, presence_penalty=1.5, and temperature=1.0 were used. (Language table)\n> All other benchmarks adopted the same sampling configuration but with temperature=0.6 under the thinking mode.\n> Under the non-thinking mode, the sampling parameters were set to top_p=0.8, top_k=20, presence_penalty=1.5, and temperature=0.7. (Vision table)\n\nCard configs used by this replication (harness/configs/):\n- config-A.json (anchor-style trap, SKILL.md:65): thinking, temperature 0.6, top_p 0.95,\n  top_k 20, presence_penalty 1.5 — the card's thinking-mode benchmark settings.\n- config-B.json (card config, DME-0 / SKILL.md:188: card_default_mode non-thinking,\n  card_temp 0.7): non-thinking, temperature 0.7, top_p 0.8, top_k 20, presence_penalty 1.5\n  — the card's non-thinking benchmark settings.\nNote: the two configs differ in mode, temperature AND top_p — live evidence for the C1\nproposal that a two-field config gate under-covers the real diff.\n\n## Output length recommendation (Best Practices, item 2)\n> We recommend using an output length of 32,768 tokens for most queries.\n\n(The anchor's 32,768-token limit, SKILL.md:8, is card-conformant. The stage-1 probe cap\nof 4096 is a declared CPU-cost deviation; loops remain detectable at the lower cap.)\n\n## Mode switching (Thinking Mode section)\n> Qwen3.5 does not officially support the soft switch of Qwen3, i.e., `/think` and `/no_think`.\n\nMode is set via `enable_thinking` (chat-template kwarg; confirmed present in the cached\ntokenizer_config.json). The probe uses exactly this mechanism.\n\n## Math prompt standard (Best Practices, item 3)\n> Math Problems: Include \"Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\" in the prompt.\n\n## Architecture (Model Overview; config.json)\nCausal LM with vision encoder; 0.8B parameters; hidden 1024; 24 layers; hybrid layout\n6 x (3 x (Gated DeltaNet -> FFN) -> 1 x (Gated Attention -> FFN)); context 262,144.\nCross-check: 2 layers x 64 columns x 1024 hidden = 131,072 = the anchor's edited surface (S:8).\n"}
